      "text": "PostgreSQL is the de facto standard for open-source relational databases. It extends ANSI SQL more aggressively than any other RDBMS. If you're coming from SQL Server, the syntax is 90% the same — the gaps are mostly in proprietary T-SQL extensions vs PostgreSQL extensions."
